# Supabase + offline

Saavi is **not** a local-only app. Local storage exists so the product works **offline**; it is a cache / runtime mirror, not the product architecture.

## Source of truth

- **Supabase Auth**: every user has an identity (`auth.users`). Anonymous is a temporary on-ramp; ship toward Sign in with Apple / linked identity. Do not design features that assume “no auth forever.”
- **Supabase Postgres (+ RLS)**: durable shared state: households, membership, domain rows, AI usage counters, recovery. Prefer row-level sync (`docs/SYNC_ARCHITECTURE.md`) over growing the legacy `life_stores` JSON blob.
- **RevenueCat**: subscription entitlement source of truth; mirror plan onto the user/household in Supabase for server enforcement (Talk caps, invites).
- **Local (AsyncStorage / later SQLite)**: offline reads/writes, outbox, device-only prefs (app lock, biometrics). Sync when online.

## AI / Talk / Ask

- OpenAI spend caps must be enforced **server-side** (chat API + Supabase counter), keyed by authenticated user (and household for Family shared pools).
- Client-side counters are UX / offline mirror only, never the sole cost guard.
- Chat proxy must accept a **Supabase access token**, not only a shared static proxy token.

## Anti-patterns

- Shipping “final” plan/AI/invite limits that live only in AsyncStorage.
- Treating anonymous backup as a substitute for real auth.
- Blocking core CRUD on network: offline capability stays; cloud features (Talk AI, sync, media) require connectivity + auth session.
